\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces X7 provenance ablation, offline retrieval replay on the 210-question gate set. Arms 1--4 form a clean channel ablation: only \texttt  {enabled\_channels} differs, so any recall delta is attributable to that channel set. Arms 5 (evidence-bound agent, gate ON) and 6 (unsurfaced evidence, gate relaxed) reuse arm~4's five-channel ranking and are retrieval-identical to arm~4; their distinguishing columns (QA accuracy, unsupported-answer rate, mean evidence tokens) require the LLM agent run and are pending. The evidence-gate plumbing was proved offline: with the gate ON, submitting an unsurfaced turn is rejected; with the gate relaxed the same submission is accepted (\texttt  {plumbing\_ok}=true). In the deployed MAB runs the gate fired as designed: 14/1074 questions in the deployed $v2$ skill-agent run had an evidence submission rejected as unsurfaced (9/767 in $v1$); 11 of the 14 resubmitted tool-surfaced evidence inside the loop and the remaining 3 ended at the step cap and were answered from tool-surfaced context; zero rejections on the LME runs{}. Bootstrap CIs: 2{,}000 resamples, 95\%.}}{18}{table.caption.24}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:provenance-ablation}{{6}{18}{X7 provenance ablation, offline retrieval replay on the 210-question gate set. Arms 1--4 form a clean channel ablation: only \texttt {enabled\_channels} differs, so any recall delta is attributable to that channel set. Arms 5 (evidence-bound agent, gate ON) and 6 (unsurfaced evidence, gate relaxed) reuse arm~4's five-channel ranking and are retrieval-identical to arm~4; their distinguishing columns (QA accuracy, unsupported-answer rate, mean evidence tokens) require the LLM agent run and are pending. The evidence-gate plumbing was proved offline: with the gate ON, submitting an unsurfaced turn is rejected; with the gate relaxed the same submission is accepted (\texttt {plumbing\_ok}=true). In the deployed MAB runs the gate fired as designed: \GateRejectStats {}. Bootstrap CIs: 2{,}000 resamples, 95\%}{table.caption.24}{}}
\newlabel{tab:provenance-ablation@cref}{{[table][6][2147483647]6}{[1][17][]18}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Results on other benchmarks under their stated test procedures; each row states its answerer and judge. The LoCoMo run differs from Mem0's published $J$ in two admitted ways---single run versus 10-run mean$\pm $std, and the answerer/judge model---and carries a disclosed legacy-fingerprint caveat; we state these conditions so the comparison is reproducible. The LME source-reading agent track's two extra questions follow its session evidence rule; comparisons are made only within the same track.}}{18}{table.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
